Title: EZproxy source takes the wrong PDF link on publisher landing pages
Created: 2026-11-11
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-11-11T21:38Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

Observed on 2026-11-11 with v0.3.0, `--source ezproxy`, on a list of paywalled
DOIs for a literature review, with a valid BibCNRS proxy session: the same
cookie file fetched the publishers' PDFs when their address was requested
directly through the proxy. Reported from the climate-finance-het project
(its ticket 2882).

Observations, each reproduced once:

- **Taylor & Francis**, `10.1080/14693062.2022.2080634`: "downloaded file is
  not a valid PDF". The proxied landing page (HTTP 200) has no
  `citation_pdf_url` meta tag, so `_extract_pdf_link` falls back to the first
  `href` containing `.pdf`. On this page that is an external press release
  cited in the article's reference list. The publisher's own address,
  `/doi/pdf/<doi>?download=true` on the proxied host, returns the PDF.
- **Wiley**, `10.1111/rode.12271` and `10.1111/dech.12779`: same message.
  `/doi/pdfdirect/<doi>?download=true` on the proxied host returns the PDF.
  Which link the tool followed was not traced.
- **DOI resolution**, `10.1108/emh.1999.10.5.57.1` and `10.21201/2020.6621`:
  the error names `https://doi-org.<proxy base>/<doi>` ("refusing https ->
  http redirect"). When `_resolve_publisher_url` fails it returns the doi.org
  address, which is then rewritten as a proxied host.

Why it matters beyond a failed fetch: when the first `.pdf` link on a landing
page is a real PDF, the source saves another document under the requested
work's name, and the success log does not show it. No such case was observed;
the code path allows it.

Hosts the proxy does not serve answered 404 (`10.1596`, `10.1073`, `10.1787`,
`10.5089`): expected, though the message does not say so.

## Choices

- Fix the extraction rather than add a publisher table only: the fallback is
  the defect, the patterns are a convenience (reporter's recommendation; the
  maintainer decides).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] No fallback to an arbitrary `.pdf` link: a candidate is accepted only if it points at the publisher's host (proxied or not); a fixture page whose first `.pdf` link is an external reference yields "no PDF link found", not a download
- [ ] Taylor & Francis and Wiley landing pages lead to the article PDF, tested offline with fixtures
- [ ] A failed DOI resolution fails with its own message and is not rewritten through the proxy
- [ ] A host the proxy answers 404 for is reported as not served by the proxy

## Related, not in scope

The EZproxy settings are read from the environment only. A key file read by
default, as for ISTEX, would spare callers a `source` step.
